-- title:
--   Inverse unipotent level automorphism scales Laurent coefficients by uⁿ
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q \ge 5$ and $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$ with $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) $(q\ell)\,M'$, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$. Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $s \in \mathbb{Z}$ and let $\tau$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` for the matrix $(T^s)^{-1}$ at $\xi$: for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ with $p_g \neq 0$ as a Laurent series, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,(T^s)^{-1}$ equals that of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,(T^s)^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\gamma$ is $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/m \\ mc & d\end{pmatrix}$ for $\gamma = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d\end{pmatrix}$. The conclusion: there exists a unit $u \in A$ such that for all $w \in K$ and all $n \in \mathbb{Z}$, the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $\tau w$ equals $u^n$ (read in $L$) times the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $w$.
--
--   The element $(T^s)^{-1}$ conjugated by $\mathrm{diag}(q\ell,1)$ acts as the translation $z \mapsto z - s/(q\ell)$, which multiplies the $n$-th $q$-expansion coefficient by a $(q\ell)$-th root of unity raised to the $n$-th power; the statement records this as a coefficientwise scaling by a unit of the discrete valuation ring $A$, valid on all of $K$ and not merely on the generating ratios of integral forms. It is used to show that the automorphism $\tau$ preserves the condition that all Laurent coefficients lie in the maximal ideal of $A$, in the auxiliary-level analysis of the full-level function field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevel_exists_isUnit_forall_coeff_apply_eq_pow_mul_coeff_of_isLevelAutAt_T_zpow_inv.lean

